---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service | CraftGrid"
  description="CraftGrid prototype platform terms of service and milestone escrow guidelines."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 md:py-16 space-y-8">
    
    <div class="border-b border-border pb-4">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-black text-dark tracking-tight">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-secondary mt-1">Last revised: September 2025</p>
    </div>

    <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-border text-slate-700 text-xs font-medium leading-relaxed">
      Welcome to CraftGrid. By accessing or using our marketplace platform, you agree to comply with and be bound by the following terms, conditions, and escrow policies.
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-sm text-secondary space-y-4 text-xs leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-dark">1. Marketplace Purpose</h2>
      <p>
        CraftGrid provides a specialized two-sided marketplace enabling clients to connect with independent website builders, designers, developers, and web agencies for packaged services and custom website project briefs.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-dark">2. Milestone Escrow & Payments</h2>
      <p>
        All orders processed through CraftGrid utilize milestone-based escrow custody. Clients authorize project funding upfront, and funds are disbursed to builders strictly upon explicit milestone approval in the Order Workspace.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-dark">3. Platform Fees</h2>
      <p>
        CraftGrid charges a standard 5% platform administration fee on client milestone deposits to maintain escrow infrastructure, identity verification, and dispute resolution workflows.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-dark">4. Intellectual Property & Code Ownership</h2>
      <p>
        Upon final approval of project milestones and full release of agreed funds, all custom website design assets, Liquid templates, Webflow projects, and codebase deliverables transfer to the purchasing client.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>
